meta {
  name: Get Product by SKU (Invalid Identifier)
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{pim_base_url_v3}}/products/BAG-10157
  body: none
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Authorization: Bearer {{access_token}}
  Accept: application/json
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 422
  res.body.errors[0].name: eq ValidationError
}

docs {
  Confirmed live 2026-09-07 against "David's Dev Account". Trigger case --
  intentionally uses a SKU (`BAG-10157`) instead of the Mongo ObjectId as
  the `{identifier}` path segment.

  ## Spec/docs discrepancy found -- important
  `API V3.md` explicitly documents `GET /products/<identifier>` as
  accepting **either** the Mongo ID or the `sku`. This is **false for this
  v3 endpoint/account**: passing a SKU returns
  `422 {"errors":[{"name":"ValidationError","description":"...Id must be
  of type PydanticObjectId..."}]}`. Only the raw ObjectId works (see
  "Get Product by ID.bru" in this folder). Flag to Plytix -- this may be a
  v1-only behavior `API V3.md` incorrectly carried over to v3, or a
  feature this account/endpoint doesn't have enabled.

  This is also the confirmed shape of a 422 validation error on a GET
  path-param mismatch: `errors` is a flat array of
  `{name, description}`, distinct from the nested `error.msg`/
  `errors[].field` shape documented (and confirmed) for the 401 auth
  error in `01-Authentication/`.
}
